---
layout: layouts/product.njk
permalink: /phone/applications/desktop/windows/
title: "VoiceTel Phone for Windows — Install Guide & FAQ"
description: "Download, install, and troubleshoot VoiceTel Phone and VoiceML Phone on Windows (installer .exe, portable .exe, or .zip). SHA-256 checksums, first-launch walkthrough, and FAQ."
platform: windows
---
{%- from "partials/v2/macros.njk" import arrow %}
{%- set voicetel = phoneApps.apps | where("key", "voicetel") | first %}
{%- set winSetup = voicetel.desktop | where("platform", "windows") | where("format", "Installer (.exe)") | first %}
{%- set winPortable = voicetel.desktop | where("platform", "windows") | where("format", "Portable (.exe)") | first %}
{%- set winZip = voicetel.desktop | where("platform", "windows") | where("format", ".zip") | first %}

<section class="hero hero--page" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
	<div class="hero__bg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
	<div class="container hero__inner">
		<div class="hero__copy">
			<p class="eyebrow">Desktop &middot; Windows</p>
			<h1 id="hero-heading">VoiceTel Phone for Windows.</h1>
			<p class="lede">Download, install, and troubleshoot the Windows app: installer, portable executable, or .zip archive. VoiceML Phone, the same softphone for VoiceML accounts, is listed alongside.</p>
			<div class="cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary btn--lg" href="#download">Download for Windows {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost btn--lg" href="/phone/applications/desktop/">All desktop clients</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<div class="hero__visual">
			{%- set kpis = [
				{ label: "Version", value: voicetel.version, sub: "Built " ~ voicetel.built },
				{ label: "Installer", value: winSetup.size, sub: ".exe · setup wizard and Start-menu shortcut" },
				{ label: "Portable", value: winPortable.size, sub: ".exe · no install, run the executable directly" },
				{ label: "Archive", value: winZip.size, sub: ".zip · extract and run VoiceTel.exe, no installer" }
			] %}
			{% include "partials/v2/kpi-grid.njk" %}
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="download" aria-labelledby="download-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">1 &middot; Download</p>
			<h2 id="download-heading">Choose the build that suits your deployment.</h2>
			<p class="lede">If you're unsure, use the <strong>installer (.exe)</strong>: a standard setup wizard that adds a Start-menu shortcut. The <strong>portable .exe</strong> runs with no install, and the <strong>.zip</strong> extracts with no installer; run <code>VoiceTel.exe</code> inside it.</p>
		</div>
		{%- for app in phoneApps.apps %}
		{%- set files = app.desktop | where("platform", platform) %}
		<h3 class="subsection-heading" id="download-{{ app.key }}">{{ app.name }} {{ app.version }}</h3>
		<div class="prose"><p>{{ app.audience }}</p></div>
		<div class="table-container">
			<table class="data-table">
				<thead>
					<tr><th scope="col">Build</th><th scope="col">SHA-256</th></tr>
				</thead>
				<tbody>
					{%- for file in files %}
					<tr>
						<td>{{ file.format }} &middot; {{ file.arch }}<br><a href="{{ phoneApps.baseUrl }}{{ file.file }}">{{ file.file }}</a> &middot; {{ file.size }}</td>
						<td><code class="mono">{{ file.sha256 | replace(r/^(.{32})/, "$1<wbr>") | safe }}</code></td>
					</tr>
					{%- endfor %}
				</tbody>
			</table>
		</div>
		{%- endfor %}
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="verify" aria-labelledby="verify-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">2 &middot; Verify checksum</p>
				<h2 id="verify-heading">Compare the SHA-256 before you install.</h2>
				<p class="lede">Optional: validate file integrity by comparing SHA-256 checksums. Open Windows PowerShell, run the command against the file you downloaded, and compare the output with the value listed above.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual">
				{%- set code %}{% highlight "powershell" %}Get-FileHash .\VoiceTel-{{ voicetel.version }}-Setup.exe -Algorithm SHA256
# substitute whichever file you downloaded;
# the Hash must match the checksum listed above{% endhighlight %}{% endset %}
				{%- set terminal = { label: "Windows PowerShell", pill: "SHA-256", code: code } %}
				{% include "partials/v2/terminal.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--tint" id="install" aria-labelledby="install-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="row row--reverse">
			<div class="row__text">
				<p class="eyebrow">3 &middot; Install and first launch</p>
				<h2 id="install-heading">Run the installer, allow the microphone, sign in.</h2>
				<p class="lede">The installer walks through a setup wizard; the portable .exe and the .zip run in place. On first launch, allow microphone access and enter the credentials for your account.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="row__visual" id="firstlaunch">
				{%- set steps = [
					{ title: "Run the installer", body: "Double-click the downloaded <strong>-Setup.exe</strong> file. For the portable build, run the <strong>.exe</strong> directly, or extract the <strong>.zip</strong> and run the app inside it." },
					{ title: "Pass SmartScreen", body: "If Windows SmartScreen appears, click <em>More info</em>, then <em>Run anyway</em>." },
					{ title: "Finish the wizard", body: "Follow the installation wizard to complete setup." },
					{ title: "Open the app", body: "Open <strong>VoiceTel</strong> (or <strong>VoiceML Phone</strong>) from the Start Menu." },
					{ title: "Allow microphone access", body: "Allow access when prompted. If you missed the prompt, go to <em>Settings &rarr; Privacy &amp; security &rarr; Microphone</em>, enable <em>Microphone access</em>, and allow the app." },
					{ title: "Sign in", body: "Enter your VoiceTel SIP credentials (username, password, display name) as provisioned in the customer portal. In VoiceML Phone, enter your VoiceML activation code under <em>Settings &rarr; Auto Provision</em> instead." }
				] %}
				{% include "partials/v2/step-list.njk" %}
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section section--white" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
	<div class="container">
		<div class="section__head">
			<p class="eyebrow">FAQ</p>
			<h2 id="faq-heading">Questions about VoiceTel Phone on Windows.</h2>
		</div>
		{%- set faqs = [
			{ q: "How do I uninstall or repair the app?", a: "Open <em>Settings &rarr; Apps &rarr; Installed apps</em>. Locate <strong>VoiceTel</strong> and choose <em>Uninstall</em> or <em>Modify/Repair</em> if available." },
			{ q: "What if audio doesn’t work?", a: "Check input/output devices in Windows Sound settings and verify microphone permissions are enabled." },
			{ q: "Where can I find logs?", a: "Logs are stored in <code>%APPDATA%\\VoiceTelPhone\\logs</code>. You can share them with support if needed." },
			{ q: "Why does the installer request admin rights?", a: "Admin privileges are required to register audio components and add VoiceTel Phone to the Start Menu." },
			{ q: "Can I install without admin rights?", a: "Yes &mdash; use the portable executable (.exe) or the .zip archive above." },
			{ q: "Upgrading from an earlier version?", a: "Fully quit the running app from the system tray (right-click &rarr; <em>Quit</em>) before installing; otherwise the single-instance lock re-focuses the old version." }
		] %}
		{% include "partials/v2/faq.njk" %}

		<div class="cta-band">
			<div class="cta-band__text">
				<h3 class="cta-band__title">Need credentials first?</h3>
				<p class="cta-band__body">Sign up to provision SIP credentials, then install VoiceTel Phone on every Windows workstation that needs to make calls.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="cta-band__actions cta-row">
				<a class="btn btn--primary" href="/signup/">Free trial {{ arrow(14) }}</a>
				<a class="btn btn--ghost" href="/phone/applications/desktop/">All desktop clients</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>
